      "n_chars": 57,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Comparison with published incident-AF models}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0078",
      "sha256": "952172146d140bc6662c537892e1e4a79c1e4e3febbc838b908b766b7e576a5e",
      "char_start": 38988,
      "char_end": 39762,
      "n_chars": 774,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Four results answer the research question within one health system. BTTN with the clinical term had the highes"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0079",
      "sha256": "af3e054ee390163615064ff4fdc739b3c26744aaf89a1772bd78c5a7161a97ca",
      "char_start": 39764,
      "char_end": 40632,
      "n_chars": 868,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Published results give context for these values but do not rank them. On the hospital behind MIMIC-IV, a survi"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0080",
      "sha256": "738bc42f4e2711fcf5d5669774565c1d2dd9b41c0e3f07b48311fd34cfb50d76",
      "char_start": 40634,
      "char_end": 41438,
      "n_chars": 804,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The gain of the fused model over the clinical model agrees with reports that ECG and clinical information are "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0081",
      "sha256": "b89270e9d04f13ddd869b1a8089aa84e95c66a44945faed9ccc368701bacddfd",
      "char_start": 41440,
      "char_end": 41518,
      "n_chars": 78,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Implications of a readable ECG term with a separate clinical term}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0082",
      "sha256": "5b361964e94e8baed0d7a2f1e5cc390ca7be1452fe2eca8541fba2dacabd82b1",
      "char_start": 41520,
      "char_end": 42243,
      "n_chars": 723,
      "section": "Implications of a readable ECG term with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Separating the clinical term from the block-term layer lets the fused model gain discrimination without changi"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0083",
      "sha256": "aa4c873667696bb1141a95af7f84d528a136d7235b2db9c20469899db1d43d9d",
      "char_start": 42245,
      "char_end": 43294,
      "n_chars": 1049,
      "section": "Implications of a readable ECG term with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The PR-window concentration of the occlusion profile is in line with saliency reports of other incident-AF mod"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0084",
      "sha256": "10593d2d0f12e3569fe1c143163924ec1f2a2ff95ee4401fe35219a8384e55b9",
      "char_start": 43296,
      "char_end": 44184,
      "n_chars": 888,
      "section": "Implications of a readable ECG term with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The association is not uniform, and the comparison has a limited scope. In a Swedish cohort of 70-year-olds, t"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0085",
      "sha256": "e1cf272f8e1ace63bffd6ed386f04cf9d693fcd6f1444b758269bc90d8b87019",
      "char_start": 44186,
      "char_end": 44784,
      "n_chars": 598,
      "section": "Implications of a readable ECG term with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "An atrial focus also has a clinical frame. An expert consensus describes atrial cardiomyopathy as a set of str"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0086",
      "sha256": "d0decde1f4e8cd70496fdbd60b2ab02709d4188d70236a8169f6abe155706000",
      "char_start": 44786,
      "char_end": 44810,
      "n_chars": 24,
      "section": "Implications of a readable ECG term with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Limitations}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0087",
      "sha256": "461a5eec297e2ce6197efc6b930c559e386d8b91cc5c8af0d47f7319b641d4bd",
      "char_start": 44812,
      "char_end": 45591,
      "n_chars": 779,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The study used one database from one health system and has no external validation in a cohort with dated outco"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0088",
      "sha256": "191bffeaea8434c55d91c964a6b8543e7753371087d0c4d77d11f6a4de0ed415",
      "char_start": 45593,
      "char_end": 46304,
      "n_chars": 711,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The comparator and the covariates have limits of their own. Age is the anchor age of MIMIC-IV, which is not th"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0089",
      "sha256": "a637bcacd8c0f2c9ebacac3834686e5462c8cd50d9635945146c064f1ca7ac36",
      "char_start": 46306,
      "char_end": 47023,
      "n_chars": 717,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The occlusion readout is a perturbation explanation of the fitted model on 120 high-risk training ECGs. It is "
    },
